{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773093295,"nonce":"1TF8lWhwGB4jHiZzCz3Ms1ouNrE=","title":"Tab bar: user-configurable layout and rearrangeable tabs","message":"The top-level tab bar (Sessions, Monitor, Auth Queue, Issues, etc.) should be user-configurable. Users should be able to:\n\n- Rearrange tabs to match their workflow\n- Pin/unpin tabs from the overflow menu\n- Possibly hide tabs they never use\n\nCurrently the layout is hardcoded. Moving the Graph tab to the overflow menu was a workaround — the real solution is giving users control over which tabs appear in the primary bar vs. overflow menu.\n\nLabels: deferred, feature","files":null}]}